<div style="background:#fff;" data-comment-anchor="f432c1c3b6-div"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>How is precision flip chip different from standard flip chip?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">The interconnect principle is the same (bumped die bonded face-down), but placement accuracy and alignment requirements are tighter for optical, RF and sensor devices where these parameters affect performance.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Which flip-chip bonding methods do you offer?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Contacted connections (ACF / ACP, NCF / NCP and SBB stud bump bonding) and metal joints (C4, ESC and GGI). Gold-to-gold interconnect (GGI) is our featured process: gold bumps bond directly to gold pads by thermo-compression or ultrasonic energy, with no solder or adhesive.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Which substrates can you bond to?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Ceramic, glass, PCB, lead frame and other substrates, from 40 × 40 mm up to 170 × 105 mm.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What die sizes and wafers does the GGI bonder handle?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">The TDK AFM-1503 handles die from 0.8 to 3.0 mm with the standard camera, down to 0.3 × 0.3 × 0.1 mm as an option. Wafer supply is 6 inches and maximum bond load is 25 N.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What placement accuracy and throughput can you achieve?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Mounting accuracy is 7 µm in X and Y and 0.3° in theta. Mounting time is 0.8 sec per shot for a standard chip and 1.6 sec for an H-Package, with capacity of around 1.2 Mpcs per month.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is the assembly verified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Verification includes 2D and 3D (CT) X-ray, placement-accuracy checks and IPC / AEC-Q reliability testing, supported by per-unit traceability.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What quality systems apply?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">ISO 9001 applies group-wide, with IATF 16949 for automotive work and ISO 13485 for medical programs, in ESD-controlled areas meeting ANSI/ESD S20.20.</div>
    </details>
    </div>
